<%# locals: (title:, crumbs: [], crumb_label: nil, meta: nil, meta_title: nil, label: nil, tabs: [], anchors: [], tabs_data: {}, menu: [], menu_label: "Links", action: nil, tools_html: nil, actions_html: nil, links: [], links_label: "More links", data: {}, row_class: "-mx-4 px-4") %>
<%# THE PAGE HEADER: the second layer of the pinned stack (docs/PAGE_HEADER.md).
    navbar, then this row, then a section's header (studio/_section_header), then a
    table's sticky header, each below the last.

    AT REST it has no background and no border: a title on the left, tabs on the
    right. ONCE STUCK under the navbar it takes the bar. Its box never changes
    between the two, so a state change moves nothing and republishes nothing.

      title         the page's one h1.
      crumbs        the trail above the title: the page's ancestors, root first, as
                    [{ label:, href: }]. studio_crumbs builds it from the app's one
                    parent map (Studio::Crumbs). The trail ends with the page itself,
                    crumb_label or else the title. Below 40rem the trail gives way to
                    one link to the parent. Every ancestor link carries
                    data-page-transition-back, so the page transition plays the
                    app's move the other way (docs/PAGE_TRANSITIONS.md).
      crumb_label   the page's own name in the trail, when the title is long.
      meta          short text beside the title, such as the version. Hidden on a
                    phone, where the tabs need the width.
      meta_title    the meta's title attribute.
      label         the pill group's nav's accessible name. A row with tabs or
                    anchors needs it.

    THE FOUR KINDS OF CONTROL on the right (docs/PAGE_HEADER.md, "The four kinds of
    control"), always in this order and at the one height of .btn-sm:

      tabs          views of the same thing (Deployments | Triage), [{ label:, href:,
                    current:, data: }]. One pill group with the gliding pill. `current`
                    is the aria-current value ("page" or "true"), blank on the others.
      anchors       sections of this page, [{ label:, href: "#id", current:, data: }].
                    The same pill group; a same-page link scrolls, with no visit. A row
                    takes tabs or anchors, never both: it has one pill group.
      tabs_data     data attributes for the pill group's scroller.
      menu          related pages elsewhere, [{ label:, href:, data: }]: one neutral
                    button, menu_label ("Links"), that opens a list of them.
      action        the page's one primary action, { label:, href:, data: }. Rightmost.
      tools_html    local-only and dev controls, after the action, muted.
      actions_html  DEPRECATED: free HTML after the pill group. It renders for one
                    release and warns once per call site in development.
      links         the page's other links, [{ label:, href:, current: }], on a line of
                    their own at the foot of the row, so they stick with it.
      links_label   that line's accessible name.
      data          data attributes for the row, such as the page's own controller.
      row_class     the bleed. The default fits a container with px-4; pass "" in a
                    container with no gutter of its own.

    NOT components/_page_header: a host's view wins over the engine's at the same
    path, and the hub has its own with other locals.

    THE ROW IS NEVER A <header>. studio/pinned_stack takes the document's first
    <header> as the navbar, so on a page with no navbar this row would publish as
    --nav-bottom.

    NOR IS IT A LANDMARK. The row is a div; the tabs, the crumbs and the links line
    are each their own <nav>, side by side, so no landmark nests in another.

    IT JOINS THE STACK WITH data-pin="page" AND POSITIONS OFF --pin-page-top, the
    bottom of everything above it. --pin-stack-bottom includes the row's own edge,
    so a row positioned off it would chase itself down the page. Anything below,
    such as the sticky table header's clone, sits under the row: the clone starts
    at the stack's bottom edge, never above it, and stacks two rungs under the
    row's --z-sticky (studio/sticky_table_header.css).

    THE SENTINEL stays at the row's place in the flow, and the row's distance from
    it is what "stuck" means, on every kind of header. It is absolutely positioned,
    so a space-y parent adds nothing for it. In a flex or grid parent it sits at the
    parent's start, so the controller measures the row's place from the row. It
    carries the controller, so the row keeps its data-studio-controller for the
    page's own. So the row carries no top margin: the space above it belongs to its
    container.

    SELF-STYLED, IN A PLAIN-CSS APP. studio_page_header_assets renders the row's own
    CSS and script once per page, only where config.page_header_self_styled asks
    (Studio::PageHeaderHelper). Everywhere else it is nil, and it sits on the
    sentinel's line, so a Tailwind app's row is the same to the byte.

    THE PAGE'S ONE H1 is this row's title, so it records one, and the navbar draws its
    brand as a div (StudioNavbarHelper#studio_page_has_h1?). content_for, not the helper:
    a host renders this partial from views that may not include the engine's helpers. It
    sits on the same line and renders nothing. %>
<% content_for(:studio_page_h1, "1") unless content_for?(:studio_page_h1) %><%= studio_page_header_assets if respond_to?(:studio_page_header_assets) %><div class="page-header-sentinel" data-studio-controller="page-header" aria-hidden="true"></div>
<%= tag.div(class: "page-header sticky #{row_class}".strip,
      style: "top: var(--pin-page-top, var(--nav-bottom, var(--nav-h, 0px))); z-index: var(--z-sticky, 30)",
      data: data.merge(pin: "page")) do %>
  <% if crumbs.any? %>
    <% parent = crumbs.last %>
    <div class="page-header-trail">
      <nav class="page-header-crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <ol>
          <% crumbs.each do |crumb| %>
            <li><%= link_to crumb.fetch(:label), crumb.fetch(:href), class: "page-header-crumb", data: { page_transition_back: "" } %></li>
          <% end %>
          <li><span class="page-header-crumb-current" aria-current="page"><%= crumb_label.presence || title %></span></li>
        </ol>
      </nav>
      <%= link_to parent.fetch(:href), class: "page-header-parent", data: { page_transition_back: "" },
            aria: { label: "Back to #{parent.fetch(:label)}" } do %><span aria-hidden="true">&lsaquo;</span> <%= parent.fetch(:label) %><% end %>
    </div>
  <% end %>
  <div class="page-header-lead">
    <h1 class="page-header-title"><%= title %></h1>
    <% if meta.present? %>
      <p class="page-header-meta label-upper"<%= %( title="#{ERB::Util.h(meta_title)}").html_safe if meta_title.present? %>><%= meta %></p>
    <% end %>
  </div>
  <% raise ArgumentError, "studio/_page_header takes tabs: or anchors:, not both (one pill group)" if tabs.any? && anchors.any? %>
  <% raise ArgumentError, "studio/_page_header takes one action: a Hash { label:, href: }" unless action.nil? || action.is_a?(Hash) %>
  <% pills, pill_kind = tabs.any? ? [tabs, "tabs"] : [anchors, "anchors"] %>
  <% if pills.any? %>
    <%= tag.nav(class: "page-header-tabs", aria: { label: label.presence }, data: { page_header_kind: pill_kind }.merge(tabs_data)) do %>
      <%# The glide: one pill, drawn once, that CSS anchors to the tab with aria-current and
          slides from tab to tab (engine.css, "The gliding pill"). Each tab keeps its own
          fill where the browser has no anchor positioning. %>
      <div class="page-header-track">
        <% pills.each do |tab| %>
          <%= link_to tab.fetch(:href),
                class: "page-header-tab btn btn-sm #{tab[:current].present? ? 'btn-primary' : 'btn-neutral'}",
                aria: { current: tab[:current].presence },
                data: tab.fetch(:data, {}) do %><span class="page-header-tab-label"><%= tab.fetch(:label) %></span><% end %>
        <% end %>
        <span class="page-header-glide btn btn-sm btn-primary" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>
  <% if actions_html.present? && defined?(Studio::PageHeader) && Studio::PageHeader.warning_enabled? %>
    <% site = caller_locations.find { |loc| loc.path.to_s.end_with?(".erb") && !loc.path.to_s.end_with?("_page_header.html.erb") } %>
    <% Studio::PageHeader.deprecate_actions_html(site: site && "#{site.path}:#{site.lineno}") %>
  <% end %>
  <% if [actions_html, tools_html].any?(&:present?) || menu.any? || action.present? %>
    <%# One cluster, in the fixed order: the old free HTML where it always stood, then
        the menu, then the action, then the tools. Each control is .btn-sm, so all
        four kinds share one height. %>
    <div class="page-header-actions">
      <%= actions_html if actions_html.present? %>
      <% if menu.any? %>
        <%# A disclosure, not role="menu": a list of links that Tab walks. The browser's
            popover opens it from the button, closes it on Escape or a click outside,
            and gives focus back to the button, with no script. The page-header
            controller adds aria-expanded, and places the list where the browser has
            no anchor positioning. %>
        <% menu_id = "page-header-menu-#{SecureRandom.hex(4)}" %>
        <div class="page-header-menu" data-page-header-kind="menu">
          <button type="button" class="page-header-menu-button btn btn-sm btn-neutral"
                  popovertarget="<%= menu_id %>" aria-controls="<%= menu_id %>"><%= menu_label %><span class="page-header-menu-caret" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div id="<%= menu_id %>" class="page-header-menu-list" popover="auto">
            <ul>
              <% menu.each do |item| %>
                <li><%= link_to item.fetch(:label), item.fetch(:href), class: "page-header-menu-item", data: item.fetch(:data, {}) %></li>
              <% end %>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      <% end %>
      <% if action.present? %>
        <%= link_to action.fetch(:label), action.fetch(:href),
              class: "page-header-action btn btn-sm btn-primary",
              data: { page_header_kind: "action" }.merge(action.fetch(:data, {})) %>
      <% end %>
      <% if tools_html.present? %>
        <div class="page-header-tools" data-page-header-kind="tools"><%= tools_html %></div>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  <% end %>
  <% if links.any? %>
    <nav class="page-header-links" aria-label="<%= links_label %>">
      <% links.each do |link| %>
        <%= link_to link.fetch(:label), link.fetch(:href), class: "page-header-link",
              aria: { current: link[:current].presence }, data: link.fetch(:data, {}) %>
      <% end %>
    </nav>
  <% end %>
<% end %>
